{%- comment -%}
  Echoes a string with the final space replaced by a no-break space, so the last
  word can never be left standing alone on a line.

  "Digital Interactive Edition" in a narrow cart column wraps to
  "DIGITAL INTERACTIVE / EDITION", and a single stranded word is exactly what
  docs/design/LINE-BREAKS.md rule 5 forbids. Gluing the last two words makes it
  break as "DIGITAL / INTERACTIVE EDITION" instead: two words on the second
  line, no orphan, and nothing about the wording changes.

  It does nothing to a one-word string, and nothing at widths where the text
  fits on one line anyway.

  Accepts: text (required)

  Usage: {%- render 'wui-tail-nbsp', text: option.value -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign words = text | strip | split: ' '
  if words.size > 1
    assign cut = words.size | minus: 1
    assign head = words | slice: 0, cut | join: ' '
    assign tail = words | last
    echo head | append: ' ' | append: tail
  else
    echo text
  endif
-%}
